# FullShot — .gitattributes
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS AT ALL
#
# Every one of the 245 text files in this tree is LF-only today, on Windows.
# (Measured, not assumed: zero 0x0D bytes across the whole tree excluding
# node_modules, .claude and Reference.)
#
# Git for Windows installs with `core.autocrlf=true` by default. Without this
# file, the first clone on a second machine would check every one of those
# files out with CRLF endings. Nothing would look broken: the extension would
# still load, the sims would still pass. But every shipped file's bytes would
# differ from the bytes that were audited, `node publish/package.node.js`
# would produce a zip with a different md5 from the one reviewed, and the
# project's TEETH doctrine — "restore byte-identical, verify md5" — would be
# quietly false on that machine only.
#
# That is precisely the failure shape this project keeps getting bitten by: a
# claim that stays green locally while being wrong somewhere nobody looked.
# One line prevents it.

# Normalize to LF in the repository AND on checkout, on every platform,
# regardless of the cloner's core.autocrlf setting.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries: never touched, never diffed as text, never line-ending-converted.
# (`text=auto` already infers this from NUL bytes; stating it removes the
# inference — a zip whose first bytes happen to look textual cannot be
# misclassified.)
*.png   -text
*.jpg   -text
*.jpeg  -text
*.gif   -text
*.webp  -text
*.ico   -text
*.zip   -text
*.crx   -text
*.xpi   -text
*.woff  -text
*.woff2 -text
